  "note": "The Wilson household at Springdale, Clare Valley (#66), on the 1911 return, transcribed by A. Hagues. Springdale held no census record for any year. Wright's Directory of Nottingham prints 'Springdale, Wilson James Calvert, surveyor' on Clare Valley in 1910-11, 1913-14 and 1915-16.\n\nThe two visitors are Richardsons. Arthur Whitby Richardson, wholesale grocer, is already in the record (#1546, born 1888, at 3 Lenton Avenue in 1921) and is bound by number. Donald Hickling Richardson, bank clerk, born about 1893, is added new: the record's Donald S Richardson of Grove House, Clare Valley in 1921 is born 1888 with a different middle initial, so they are not joined on this evidence. Edith Wilson (#569, born 1884) of Western Terrace is a different woman from both Ediths here. The servant's surname is as transcribed, Wathing. Ages are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way.",
  "source": "1911 census, Springdale, Clare Valley, transcribed by A. Hagues. Directory evidence: Wright's Directory of Nottingham 1910-11, page 69 (Leicester Special Collections id 165745); 1913-14, page 80 (id 166436); 1915-16, page 82 (id 347723).",
